    "was": "'The Green' appears TWICE — once by the house, once on the open fairway. Two different places with the same name, or one of them a stray? They need distinct ids before either can be traced.",
    "ruling": "The SECOND 'The Green' — bottom-centre, on the open fairway — was an ERROR in the annotation, not a second place. Retired. The surviving 'The Green' is the one near the house (id the-green-house), which Paul traced with 20 points. Recorded rather than deleted so a later reader does not re-derive the duplicate from the annotated image and think a name was lost."
   },
   {
    "date": "2026-08-31",
    "by": "paul-stated",
    "was": "There is NO standalone 'Fairway' label any more",
    "ruling": "KEEP the old Fairway zone. paul-stated 2026-08-31: it simply was not re-labelled during the annotation. The big open area is still hers and still called Fairway; it is not superseded by 'The Green' and it is not out of scope. This also answers the acreage question — the traced 0.6 acres is the garden complex, and Fairway is additional."
   },
   {
    "date": "2026-08-31",
