  "geometryGap": {
   "found": "2026-08-31, from Paul's rulings on two roster entries.",
   "statement": "The record has ONE geometry type — the polygon — and at least two of the things Mom named are not areas. 'Upper-Uber Wall Area' is a wall ('more of a dividing line than a zone') and 'The Path' is, in Paul's words, 'the same shape. More of a landmark than a zone.'",
   "consequence": "'The Path' is currently recorded as a 17-vertex POLYGON. That is not a bad trace; it is a MIS-MODELLING — a line forced into an area, which then reports an acreage and a median slope that mean nothing. The same pressure produced the name 'Upper-Uber Wall Area' years earlier.",
   "alsoMissing": "Paths, walls, the driveway, water lines, fences and the property line itself are all linear. None can be recorded today.",
   "doNot": "Do not fold 'The Path' into zones.json as a polygon to make the set tidy."
